          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260808_163843_21d31f85-8f4f-438a-80cc-f34569d6014d.png",
            "name": "Helen S.",
            "rating": 5,
            "quote": "An excellent supplement that has helped so much with my dry eyes. I was worried that my problem would only get worse. But my granddaughter told me to start taking these omega pills and wow, words can't describe how grateful I am that I found this."
          }
        },
        "photo_3": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260808_163652_c045f3c9-0fa6-4821-ad4b-5e203dcee3c9.png",
            "name": "Jeremy N.",
            "rating": 5,
            "quote": "This is the third time I've bought them. Before taking these pills my doctor was saying my eye was getting swollen and looking very dry. After taking 2 pills a day, not only do I see a difference, I feel a difference. 🙂"
          }
        },
        "photo_5": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260808_171824_9b160043-8f0f-499b-b394-303aa3f7bac3.png",
            "name": "Henry P.",
            "rating": 4.5,
            "quote": "I honestly didn't realize how much I was rubbing my eyes until I started working from home. By 3pm I'd be staring at my laptop, blinking constantly and reaching for eye drops again. I tried changing my screen brightness, taking breaks, drinking more water… nothing really stuck. I eventually started taking omega supplements because I was already trying to be more intentional about my daily routine. It's not some overnight miracle, but after keeping up with them for a while, my eyes just don't feel like the first thing I notice at the end of the day anymore. That's a win for me."
          }
        },
        "photo_6": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260808_171835_5adf15a4-0671-4757-bbc9-df58bc2c8550.png",
            "name": "Anthony N.",
            "rating": 4.5,
            "quote": "I've worn contacts for years, so I assumed the uncomfortable, dry feeling was just something I had to put up with. Some days I'd take them out as soon as I got home because my eyes were so irritated. I started paying more attention to my overall eye-care routine and added an omega supplement. I also became much better about taking breaks from my screen. I can't point to one thing and say that's what changed everything, but together my eyes have felt noticeably more comfortable. I wish I'd taken it seriously sooner."
          }
        },
        "photo_7": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260808_171805_b5df2d16-c22b-496d-aeef-afbc75374ea5.png",
            "name": "Emmah N.",
            "rating": 5,
            "quote": "For the longest time I blamed everything on getting older. My eyes would feel dry by the afternoon and I'd carry drops everywhere — in my purse, at my desk, even in the car. My sister suggested looking into omega supplements, so I added them to my morning routine. I almost stopped after the first couple weeks because I wasn't expecting anything dramatic. But eventually I realized I wasn't reaching for my drops quite as often. Now they're just part of my morning routine, along with my coffee."
          }
        },
        "photo_8": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260808_171815_1a5e8988-20e8-4b14-b69e-5cd28ac2b03d.png",
            "name": "Hannah K.",
            "rating": 5,
            "quote": "I was actually skeptical about omega supplements because I've bought so many things that promised to fix everything. I started taking these mostly because I wanted to improve my daily nutrition, not because I expected some huge transformation. The funny thing is that after a few months, I realized my dry-eye routine had gotten a lot less complicated. I wasn't constantly thinking about my eyes anymore. For me, the biggest difference was that it happened gradually enough that I almost didn't notice."
          }
        }
